    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup for May 13th is headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (65.99) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.49), who stand as our most potent options in today\u2019s slate. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a steady matchup against Robbie Ray, where his consistent production profile remains insulated despite the lefty-lefty dynamic. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** earns a top-tier score by leading off against Seth Lugo; his high xwOBA (0.391) and the favorable order placement provide the highest floor for run production today. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** (62.30) carries significant upside despite a tough draw against Max Fried. While the platoon disadvantage against Fried is non-trivial, the combination of wind blowing out and the high-leverage #2 spot in the order keeps **Gunnar Henderson** squarely in the elite tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Brady House** (49.98) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73). **Brady House** fell just short of the active roster; although he benefits from a hitter-friendly environment and a favorable breeze against Nick Lodolo, his projected efficiency simply didn\u2019t eclipse the current utility options like **Coby Mayo** (57.15). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, typically an anchor of our offense, is relegated to the bench today due to a suboptimal matchup against an elite arm (Jax), which suppresses his daily efficiency score below our threshold for activation. We remain cautious of the volatility surrounding **Heliot Ramos** (42.73), whose score has plummeted due to a brutal matchup against Shohei Ohtani; he remains in the lineup purely by virtue of roster constraints, as we monitor his performance against such high-tier pitching. \n\nOutside of our primary starters, we continue to track the health of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth flexibility. Investors should note that **Drake Baldwin** (58.87) and **Liam Hicks** (57.75) both face favorable conditions that could yield sneaky value in the Catcher slots, provided they can capitalize on the targetable ERAs of Shota Imanaga and Louie Varland, respectively. Owners should remain vigilant for official lineup confirmations, as any shifts in batting order for **Jackson Merrill** or **Nasim Nunez** could impact their efficiency ratings significantly.",
